  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Mocha Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to ensure target populations have equitable access to sufficient, safe and nutritious food. This WFP project provides emergency food transfers to targeted populations for one month, as part of a 3-month assistance package, and executes activities such as identification and selection of cyclone-affected townships and villages, provision of food assistance to targeted 90,000 people, and distribution monitoring and reporting. The project provides life-saving assistance to 90,000 people, including 31,500 women, 25,200 men, 33,300 children, and 2,700 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
